{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/376363-inhabit-plants","id":376363,"title":"Inhabit + plants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-20T10:23:13-08:00","id":376363,"title":"Inhabit + plants","content":"Do you think inhabit could be used on plants? How would you rule it? Could a wraith inhabit an ivy or a tree and use the branches as tentacles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T19:20:59-08:00","id":376831,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Since we haven't seen the Revised (TM) Arcanoi of Wr20, I can only judge based on the updated Inhabit and my recollections of of the other Arts. <br /> Short answer, I'd be inclined to say No. Inhabit seems to be a more techy-forgy type of the thing and I think manipulating trees a la Evil Dead (amiright?) might be better represented with...idk...Puppetry and Pandemonium? Maybe Flux? <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Disclaimer: The above is my off-the-cuff opinion. This sort of thing might have been covered in a Guildbook. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T04:41:47-08:00","id":377116,"title":"","content":"I totally agree with Nazfool.<br /> That said, Ferrymen can combine (two) Arcanoi in order to generate powerfull effects, maybe inhabiting plants could be one of them. In any case, only rare and powerfull wraith should be able to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:15:03-08:00","id":377337,"title":"","content":"Puppetry seems an odd choice to animate plants, and Pandemonium might work, although its purview seems to relate more to creating an attacking plant rather than control an existing one. Certainly Inhabit is not meant to work only on technological or mechanical artifacts, since it can Control houses, including Windows and doors. But i'll think about it, Thanks for the replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T12:07:48-08:00","id":377432,"title":"","content":"I would allow it. In general when questions like this come up I always err on the side of permissiveness and therefore creativity. It's not like you're spoiling the rigid realism of the setting otherwise.<br /> <br /> Besides, how else are you going to re-enact the tree scene from Evil Dead or Poltergeist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T21:54:49-08:00","id":377792,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">My opinion is based on the idea that Inhabit affects &quot;inanimate&quot; objects. Personally, I wouldn't consider trees and other living vegetation inanimate, but that's me. I won't think poorly of you if you do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T09:09:57-08:00","id":378106,"title":"","content":"<i>House of Tremere</i> has one of the original wizards who founded Ceoris becoming manifest through a monstrously animated tree after his death. That might indicate that Inhabit, Puppetry, or some combination of the two can work on plants; it could also be a unique consequence of the botched ritual he was killed in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T07:24:11-08:00","id":379012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/376363-inhabit-plants?p=377792#post377792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Personally, I wouldn't consider trees and other living vegetation inanimate, but that's me. I won't think poorly of you if you do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Very kind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So, how long ago does a tree need to have been chopped down for you to rule it's now a pile of wood? Or does someone need to build something out of it? Can the someone be a beaver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T09:00:42-08:00","id":379070,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">We've seen a preview for &quot;revised&quot; Inhabit, but I'd have to see what Pandemonium or Flux (or other Arts I can't remember right now) look like. If there is a *better* Art that deals with animating dead matter, I'd go with that one for manipulating a dead and gnarled tree.<br /> <br /> A log cabin, a catapult, a trebuchet, gallows, - hell! - even a wooden sign are all fair game.<br /> A beaver dam? <br /> That depends on the story and whether or not &quot;The Tale of the Haunted Beaver Dam&quot; would be thematically appropriate.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Again, the above is just my take on the subject. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}